                <mxCell id="k4-40" parent="1" style="fillColor=#000000;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=13;rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=16;spacingRight=16;" value="&lt;b&gt;The uncomfortable read:&lt;/b&gt; the build clearly fixes C4 (traceability, and so audit findings), and helps with effort. The two biggest numbers in the v1 value story, &lt;b&gt;penalties&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;duplicates&lt;/b&gt;, mostly trace to C1, C3, C5 and C6, which a per-invoice decision engine touches only partly or not at all.&lt;br&gt;That isn&#39;t a reason to drop the build. It&#39;s a reason to &lt;b&gt;claim only the value it can prove&lt;/b&gt;, or to widen scope on purpose (for example, a duplicate check across invoices)." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="84" width="1620" x="40" y="790" as="geometry"/>
